---
export const prerender = true;

import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '@/components/primitives/Section.astro';
import Prose from '@/components/primitives/Prose.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '@/components/primitives/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/site.config';

const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'Privacy', href: '/privacy' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  titleFull="Privacy policy | Murikah"
  description="How Murikah collects, uses, stores and protects personal data across murikah.com and services that link to this policy, including Murikah Tutor."
>
  <Section tone="surface" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} class="mb-6" />
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1
      id="page-title"
      class="mt-5 font-serif text-[length:var(--text-title)] leading-[1.06] font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-navy"
    >
      Privacy policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-slate">Last updated: 21 September 2026</p>

    <Prose class="mt-10">
      <p>
        This policy explains how Murikah ("Murikah", "we", "us" or "our") handles personal data
        when you use murikah.com and online services that link to this policy, including Murikah
        Tutor at tutor.murikah.com. It also explains the choices and rights available to you.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
      <p>
        Murikah is the data controller where we decide why and how personal data is processed.
        Some service providers process data on our behalf. For privacy questions or requests,
        contact <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Personal data we collect</h2>
      <p>The data we collect depends on how you use Murikah.</p>

      <h3>Website enquiries and subscriptions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name, organisation, role, email address and message when you contact us.</li>
        <li>Your email address and subscription preferences if you ask to receive updates.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Murikah Tutor accounts and sign-in</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Account identifiers such as username, email address, internal user ID and authentication
          status.
        </li>
        <li>
          Passwords are stored as password hashes rather than readable passwords where local
          password authentication is used.
        </li>
        <li>
          If you use Google Sign-In, we receive the basic Google account information needed to
          authenticate you and link the sign-in to a Tutor account, such as your Google account
          identifier, email address, name and profile information made available through the
          <code>openid</code>, <code>email</code> and <code>profile</code> scopes.
        </li>
        <li>
          We do not request access to your Gmail, Google Drive, Google Calendar, contacts, photos or
          other Google product content merely because you use Google Sign-In.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Tutor learning and workspace data</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Prompts, chat messages, model responses, conversation history, learning progress and
          related session metadata.
        </li>
        <li>
          Files, attachments, knowledge material and other content that you choose to upload or
          create.
        </li>
        <li>
          Generated work such as diagrams, visualisations, summaries, study material and other
          outputs.
        </li>
        <li>
          Preferences, selected learning modes, model or tool choices and configuration needed to
          continue your workspace.
        </li>
        <li>
          For guest use, temporary identifiers, guest interaction counts and browser-stored state
          used to enforce guest limits and preserve a conversation when you create or sign into an
          account.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Technical and security data</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          IP address, device or browser information, timestamps, request metadata, error information
          and security events where generated by our infrastructure.
        </li>
        <li>
          Session cookies and similar local-storage data needed for authentication, continuity,
          security, accessibility settings and product operation.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. How we use personal data</h2>
      <p>We use personal data to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>provide, operate and improve Murikah websites and services;</li>
        <li>create and secure accounts, authenticate users and maintain signed-in sessions;</li>
        <li>preserve conversations and learning progress across sessions where applicable;</li>
        <li>process prompts, files and requests and return AI-assisted results;</li>
        <li>enforce guest limits, protect against misuse and maintain service security;</li>
        <li>respond to enquiries, support requests and service communications;</li>
        <li>send marketing or newsletter messages that you have asked to receive;</li>
        <li>diagnose failures, monitor reliability and improve product performance; and</li>
        <li>comply with applicable law and protect our legal rights and users.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Our lawful bases</h2>
      <p>
        Where the Kenya Data Protection Act, 2019 applies, we rely on the lawful basis appropriate
        to the activity. This may include performing a contract or taking steps you request before a
        contract, complying with a legal obligation, our legitimate interests in operating and
        securing the service, and your consent where consent is required, including for optional
        marketing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where we rely on consent, you may withdraw it at any time. Withdrawal does not affect
        processing that was lawful before withdrawal.
      </p>

      <h2>5. AI services and your content</h2>
      <p>
        Murikah Tutor uses external AI, search, speech, media and infrastructure services to perform
        functions you request. Depending on the feature, relevant portions of your prompt,
        conversation, uploaded content or instructions may be sent to a configured service provider
        so that it can generate or retrieve the requested result.
      </p>
      <p>
        Current service categories can include infrastructure providers such as Cloudflare, AI model
        providers such as Google, NVIDIA and Alibaba Cloud/DashScope, and search or retrieval
        providers such as Tavily. The exact provider used may change as the service evolves. We aim
        to send only the information needed for the requested function and to use provider
        configurations appropriate for application/API use.
      </p>
      <p>
        Murikah does not sell your personal data. We do not use your Google account information for
        advertising, and we do not use Google Sign-In data to train a general-purpose AI model.
        Google account data obtained through Google Sign-In is used for authentication, account
        linking, security and related account functionality described in this policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not use Tutor to make solely automated decisions about you that produce legal or
        similarly significant effects.
      </p>

      <h2>6. When we share personal data</h2>
      <p>We may share personal data only where needed for the purposes described above, including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          with hosting, storage, authentication, communications, AI, search and other technology
          providers that support the service;
        </li>
        <li>
          with professional advisers where reasonably necessary for legal, security, audit or
          compliance purposes;
        </li>
        <li>
          where required by law, court order or a lawful request from a competent authority; or
        </li>
        <li>
          in connection with a genuine corporate transaction, subject to appropriate confidentiality
          and data-protection safeguards.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell or rent personal data to data brokers or advertisers.</p>

      <h2>7. International processing</h2>
      <p>
        Some service providers may process data outside Kenya. Where personal data is transferred
        internationally, we take reasonable steps to use providers and safeguards appropriate to the
        nature of the data and the applicable legal requirements. Where required, this may include
        contractual safeguards, assessment of the receiving environment or obtaining consent.
      </p>

      <h2>8. How long we keep data</h2>
      <p>
        We keep personal data only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it
        was collected, including providing the service, maintaining account continuity, resolving
        disputes, meeting legal obligations and protecting the service.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Account, conversation, learning and uploaded-content data may be retained while your
          account is active and afterwards for a limited period where needed for recovery, security,
          legal or operational reasons.
        </li>
        <li>
          Guest browser/session identifiers may persist for a limited period so guest limits and
          conversation continuity cannot be reset simply by refreshing or signing out.
        </li>
        <li>
          Authentication sessions can remain valid for an extended period and may be renewed while
          you continue using Tutor; explicit sign-out ends the current signed-in session.
        </li>
        <li>
          Newsletter contact information is kept until you unsubscribe or we stop the relevant
          mailing activity.
        </li>
        <li>
          Enquiry, security and diagnostic records are retained only as long as reasonably needed
          for support, security, troubleshooting, legal or compliance purposes.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Backups and replicated storage may take additional time to age out after data is deleted from
        active systems.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use technical and organisational measures designed to protect personal data, including
        access controls, secure authentication, encrypted network connections, secret management,
        service isolation, logging and abuse controls where appropriate. No Internet service can
        guarantee absolute security, so please avoid submitting information that is unnecessary for
        your request.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Cookies and local storage</h2>
      <p>
        Murikah uses essential cookies and browser storage to keep you signed in, protect sessions,
        remember accessibility settings, enforce guest limits and restore eligible guest work after
        sign-in. These technologies are necessary for core service operation.
      </p>
      <p>
        If we introduce non-essential advertising or analytics technologies that require consent,
        we will provide an appropriate choice before using them where required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Children</h2>
      <p>
        Murikah Tutor is not intended for children under 13. If a person under 18 uses the service,
        a parent, guardian or authorised educational institution should provide or supervise the use
        where required by applicable law. If you believe a child has provided personal data without
        appropriate authority, contact us so that we can review the situation.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Your data-protection rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on the law that applies to you, you may have rights to be informed about the use of
        your personal data, access it, correct inaccurate or misleading data, request deletion or
        erasure, object to certain processing, request restriction of processing and receive portable
        copies of eligible data.
      </p>
      <p>
        To exercise a privacy right, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We
        may need to verify your identity before acting on a request.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        We encourage you to contact us first so we can address a concern. If you are in Kenya, you
        may also raise a complaint with the Office of the Data Protection Commissioner (ODPC). Your
        right to complain to a regulator is not affected by contacting us first.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as our services, providers or legal obligations change. We will
        publish the current version on this page and update the date above. If a change materially
        affects how we use personal data, we will provide additional notice where appropriate.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions and data requests can be sent to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
